From a360cd377bf08cf7126e3fa93a9d310f72ee58f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RivonClaw CI <ci@rivonclaw.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:26:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(openclaw): rotate sessions after compaction failure

Why:
- Unrecoverable compaction failures otherwise keep routing every later turn into the same broken transcript.
- RivonClaw needs to preserve the failed transcript while moving the route to a clean successor session.

Removal:
- Drop when upstream provides equivalent bounded successor-session recovery after compaction failures.

Tests:
- apps/desktop/src/gateway/vendor-compaction-session-recovery.sentinel.test.ts
